---
layout: article
title: ChatGPT
description: Connect Appwrite to ChatGPT with the remote MCP server, OAuth, and agent skills so ChatGPT can call your project and search the docs.
faqs:
  - question: How do I connect Appwrite to ChatGPT?
    answer: Add a custom ChatGPT connector or App with the MCP URL https://mcp.appwrite.io and the server name appwrite. Then complete OAuth. Also run npx skills add appwrite/skills so ChatGPT has current SDK and CLI patterns.
  - question: Do I need an API key for the ChatGPT connector?
    answer: No. Cloud uses OAuth. You sign in to Appwrite and authorize the connector. Self-hosted Appwrite still uses a local stdio server with a project API key.
  - question: Is the ChatGPT connector the same as Codex?
    answer: No. The ChatGPT connector is for ChatGPT chat and Apps. Codex inside ChatGPT uses the Codex plugin plus `codex mcp add appwrite --url https://mcp.appwrite.io/`.
---

Use Appwrite when ChatGPT is writing an app that needs auth, databases, storage, functions, or hosting. One remote MCP server covers API actions and docs search. Do not add separate `appwrite-api` and `appwrite-docs` servers.

{% section #install-skills step=1 title="Install Appwrite skills" %}

Skills give ChatGPT current Appwrite CLI and SDK patterns. In a project directory, run:

```bash
npx skills add appwrite/skills
```

If you are using Codex inside ChatGPT, you can also install the [Appwrite Codex plugin](/docs/tooling/ai/agents/codex). Skills and MCP work together: skills teach the agent how to write Appwrite code, MCP lets it act on a live project.

{% /section %}

{% section #add-connector step=2 title="Add the ChatGPT connector" %}

ChatGPT talks to Appwrite through a custom [MCP connector](https://mcp.appwrite.io). There is nothing to install locally.

1. Open ChatGPT settings and go to **Connectors** (sometimes labeled **Apps**).
2. Create a custom connector.
3. Set the MCP server URL to:

```
https://mcp.appwrite.io
```

4. Use **appwrite** as the server name if the form asks for one.
5. Save, then connect. ChatGPT opens a browser window so you can sign in to Appwrite and authorize access.

The connector uses OAuth. You do not create an API key for Cloud. If ChatGPT cannot complete the redirect, confirm you are signed in to Appwrite Cloud and that pop-ups are allowed.

{% info title="Codex in ChatGPT" %}

For the Codex coding agent inside ChatGPT, follow the [Codex setup](/docs/tooling/ai/agents/codex) as well. Codex uses `codex mcp add appwrite --url https://mcp.appwrite.io/`. The connector above is for ChatGPT chat and Apps.

{% /info %}

{% /section %}

